#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:2
msgid "Install a license key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/all-commercial.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry, Professional, Enterprise, and "
"Enterprise Advanced plans <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:7
msgid ""
"You can use the System Console or the mmctl tools to add or change a "
"Mattermost license key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:11
msgid "Go go **System Console > About > Edition and License**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:12
msgid "Upload your license key file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:14
msgid ""
"Once the key is uploaded and installed, the details of your license are "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:18
msgid ""
"Use the :ref:`mmctl license upload <administration-guide/manage/mmctl-"
"command-line-tool:mmctl license upload>` command to upload a new license "
"or replace an existing license file with a new one. When complete, "
"restart the Mattermost server. If you're running in a :doc:`High "
"Availability </administration-guide/scale/high-availability-cluster-"
"based-deployment>` environment, the new license file must be updated to "
"every node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:26
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.11, the option to add a license is disabled when the "
"license is set using an :ref:`environment variable <administration-"
"guide/configure/environment-configuration-settings:license file "
"location>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:27
msgid ""
"Enterprise customers with the Premier Support add-on can request a "
"staging license for testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:28
msgid ""
"Removing a Mattermost Enterprise or Professional license key won't remove"
" the configuration for Enterprise settings; however, these features won't"
" function until an Enterprise or Professional license key is applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:29
msgid ""
"When you're using :doc:`High Availability </administration-guide/scale"
"/high-availability-cluster-based-deployment>`, it's critical to ensure "
"that all servers in the cluster have same Enterprise license properly "
"installed to prevent multi-node clusters from failing. An Enterprise "
"license is required for High Availability to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:30
msgid ""
"When you apply an Enterprise license key to a server previously licensed "
"for Professional, Professional features retain their configuration "
"settings in Enterprise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:31
msgid ""
"When you apply a Professional license to a server previously licensed for"
" Enterprise, Enterprise features retain their configuration but will no "
"longer be accessible for use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:34
msgid "Change an existing license key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:36
msgid ""
"You don't need to wait for your current license key to expire before "
"replacing it with a new license from Mattermost. The server only checks "
"for seat count and license end date, not the start date, so you can apply"
" a new license as soon as you receive it. However, ensure your new "
"license is for a seat count that's greater than or equal to your current "
"total number of Mattermost users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:40
msgid ""
"To review license usage before uploading a new key, go to **System "
"Console > Reporting > Site Statistics**. The **Total Activated Users** "
"field shows the primary paid seat count used for license validation. "
"Review **Single-channel Guests** separately because guests in exactly one"
" channel are tracked outside the primary paid seat count, are free up to "
"a 1:1 ratio with licensed seats, and generate warnings instead of hard "
"enforcement when that allowance is exceeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:42
msgid "Follow these steps to change your license key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:44
msgid "Go to **System Console > About > Edition and License**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:45
msgid "From Mattermost v6.7, simply upload your new license key file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:49
msgid ""
"If you're running a Mattermost release older than v6.7, select **Remove "
"Enterprise License and Downgrade Server** to clear the license from the "
"server and refresh the System Console first before uploading the new key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:52
msgid "License key storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:54
msgid ""
"Once you've uploaded your license key to your Mattermost server, it's "
"stored in your SQL database at ``mattermost.Licenses``. You can check "
"what keys are on your server by running ``select * from "
"mattermost.Licenses;``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/installing-license-key.rst:56
msgid ""
"`Book a live demo <https://mattermost.com/request-demo/>`_  or `talk to a"
" Mattermost expert <https://mattermost.com/contact-sales/>`_ to explore "
"tailored solutions for your organization's secure collaboration needs. Or"
" try Mattermost yourself with a `1-hour preview <https://mattermost.com"
"/sign-up/>`_ for instant access to a live sandbox environment."
msgstr ""

